      "why": "Baseline low-area family: one micro-rotation per cycle with a shared datapath and barrel shifters. This typically minimises area for small data widths. We search W 13-18 and N 12-24 to cover the tight accuracy boundary (max_abs_err <= 2^-10) and the upper accuracy end of the Pareto front. The wide N range is included because the shared datapath keeps area relatively insensitive to N, so extra iterations can buy accuracy cheaply. angle_guard -1..2 and frac_guard 0..2 explore the precision-area trade-off, and both rounding modes are kept to allow truncation to win if it saves area while still meeting accuracy."
    },
    {
      "budget_share": 0.5,
      "family": "unrolled_k",
      "ranges": [
        {
          "choices": [
             "trunc",
             "round"
          ],
          "high": 13,
          "low": 12,
          "param": "rounding"
        },
        {
