          "param": "frac_guard"
        },
        {
          "choices": null,
          "high": 4,
          "low": 2,
          "param": "k"
        },
        {
          "choices": null,
          "high": 18,
          "low": 13,
          "param": "data_width"
        },
        {
          "choices": null,
          "high": 24,
          "low": 12,
          "param": "n_iter"
        }
      ],
      "why": "Unrolling replaces the barrel shifter with fixed shifts, which can reduce area at larger data widths despite duplicating the adder. We focus on small k (2-4) because larger k only increases area without helping the loose throughput constraint (>=1 MSPS is already met by iterative). The same data_width, n_iter, guard, and rounding ranges as iterative allow direct area-accuracy comparison and help map the Pareto front where unrolled_k might win for larger W."
    }
  ],
  "rationale": "The spec is area-critical (min luts_plus_ffs) with a tight accuracy constraint (max_abs_err <= 2^-10) and a loose throughput constraint (>=1 MSPS). Both families easily meet throughput, so the trade-off is area versus accuracy. Accuracy depends only on data_width, n_iter, angle_guard, frac_guard, and rounding. The output LSB dictates W >= 13, and CORDIC residual angle error dictates N >= 12. Since the shared datapath in iterative keeps area fairly insensitive to N, we search a wide N range (12-24) to capture accuracy gains at low area cost. Unrolled_k with small k may become more area-efficient at larger W by eliminating the barrel shifter, so we split the budget equally to map both sides of the potential crossover."
}

{
  "decision": "stop",
  "rationale": "This is the final round, and the front is feasible and well-covered, so no further exploration is possible or useful. Evidence: 45 of 60 evaluations were feasible (39 unique), with 0% violating the throughput constraint (best 13.2 MSPS vs >=1 required) and the accuracy constraint met by the front (best max_abs_err 6.72e-05 = 2^-13.86, well under the 2^-10 limit). The Pareto front spans luts_plus_ffs 260..448 and accuracy_bits 10.6..13.9, covering a meaningful trade-off curve against the HV reference point (1500, 10), giving hypervolume 4527. The selection rule (min luts_plus_ffs) is satisfied by the iterative [data_width=15 n_iter=15 angle_guard=1 frac_guard=0 rounding=round] design at luts_plus_ffs=260, accuracy_bits=10.6, throughput 11 MSPS, max_abs_err 6.32e-04 (2^-10.63) — all constraints met. No infeasibility exists, and the budget/round cap is reached, so we stop."
  ,
  "next_plan": null
}
